irectly finalizes the physical narrative of the anomaly cancellation at the \"throat\" of the Klein bottle.\n\nThis involves proving that the KMS state $\\omega_{KMS}$ (the vacuum density matrix $\\rho_{KMS}$) is invariant under:\n1. The $V_4$ Klein symmetry group (generated by `tilt` and `switch`).\n2. The Tomita-Takesaki modular conjugation $J$ (which reflects the left and right branches of the tree).\n\n---\n\n### Drafting the GNS State on the Cantor Boundary (Option A)\n\nIf we proceed with the **GNS Mapping (Option A)**, the first step is to define the KMS state on the Cuntz generators. Here is a structural sketch of how we can define the Cuntz-KMS state and its scaling property in Lean 4, preparing the ground for the GNS representation:\n\n```lean\nimport Mathlib\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.GNSState\n\nopen Matrix Complex\n\n/-! ## The KMS State on the Cuntz Algebra -/\n\n/-- An abstract type representing the Cuntz-Clifford algebra \n    generated by the binary tree. -/\naxiom CuntzAlgebra : Type*\naxiom CuntzAlgebra.instRing : Ring CuntzAlgebra\naxiom CuntzAlgebra.instStarRing : StarRing CuntzAlgebra\n\nattribute [instance] CuntzAlgebra.instRing CuntzAlgebra.instStarRing\n\n/-- The generators of the algebra (S_L and S_R isometries). -/\naxiom S_L : CuntzAlgebra\naxiom S_R : CuntzAlgebra\n\n/-- The unique KMS state (positive linear functional) on the algebra. -/\ndef State :\u003d CuntzAlgebra →+* ℂ\n\n/-- The KMS condition at inverse temperature β \u003d ln 2. \n    This encodes the binary branching of the Cantor set, where each path \n    split halves the thermodynamic weight. -/\nstructure IsKMSState (φ : State) : Prop where\n  kms_L : ∀ (A : CuntzAlgebra), φ (S_L * A * star S_L) \u003d (1 / 2 : ℂ) * φ A\n  kms_R : ∀ (A : CuntzAlgebra), φ (S_R * A * star S_R) \u003d (1 / 2 : ℂ) * φ A\n  kms_cross_LR : ∀ (A : CuntzAlgebra), φ (S_L * A * star S_R) \u003d 0\n  kms_cross_RL : ∀ (A : CuntzAlgebra), φ (S_R * A * star S_L) \u003d 0\n\n/-- The GNS semi-inner product induced by the KMS state. -/\ndef gns_inner (φ : State) (A B : CuntzAlgebra) : ℂ :\u003d\n  φ (star B * A)\n\n/-- Theorem: The GNS inner product is positive semidefinite, \n    satisfying the foundational requirement for the GNS Hilbert space construction. -/\naxiom gns_positive_semidefinite (φ : State) (A : CuntzAlgebra) : \n  0 ≤ (gns_inner φ A A).re\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.GNSState\n```\n\n### Path Selection\n* To complete the **analytical closure** of the Hilbert space representation, we can expand the GNS construction to map these algebraic state vectors directly to the `lp` space vectors.\n* To complete the **physical symmetry proof**, we can construct the $V_4$ invariance of the vacuum state and prove the topological vanishing of the anomaly.\n\nWhich path aligns best with the current goals for the repository?",
